 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "PointMatrix() starts with no points. addPoint(row, col) places a point (adding an existing point changes nothing). A move goes from one point to any other point in the same row or the same column and costs one step. isConnected(point1, point2) returns true when both are placed points and point2 can be reached from point1 by moves (a point reaches itself). getMinSteps(start, end) returns the fewest moves from start to end, 0 when they are the same placed point, and -1 when either is not a placed point or end is unreachable. Points are [row, col] pairs.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk09-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
